      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed in PS3 with the shared IncomingCallRequests registry. Requests are indexed atomically by (account, native call ID), with a separate generation index for callbacks; repeated or concurrent RINGING/media updates reuse pending or SHOW_UI results and do not invoke addNewIncomingCall again. The already bound SystemCall is reused even in the interval between answer and CURRENT. Cancellation removes both indexes without letting an old generation affect a retry; shared waiters only abandon a pending request when the final subscriber disposes. Added 12 direct registry tests covering repeated/concurrent updates, shared cancellation, answer-before-CURRENT, early/late callbacks, retries, account isolation and termination.",
